# Binance Market Intelligence Bot — environment variables
#
# Binance market data itself never needs an API key/secret — that part
# works with zero environment variables, in dev and on Vercel alike.
#
# The two variables below are OPTIONAL and control persistence only:
#
#   - Unset (default): the app stores everything (settings, watchlist,
#     signal history, paper trades, backtests) in this browser's
#     IndexedDB. Nothing to configure, nothing to deploy.
#
#   - Set: the app stores the same data in your own Supabase project
#     instead, synced across devices/browsers signed in with the same
#     (anonymous) session. See README "Supabase setup" and
#     docs/supabase-schema.sql for the one-time setup (run the SQL file,
#     enable Anonymous Sign-Ins).
#
# Both are safe to expose to the browser (NEXT_PUBLIC_*) — they are the
# project URL and the RLS-restricted "anon" key, not a service-role key.
# NEVER put a service-role key in a NEXT_PUBLIC_ variable.

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
